\paragraph{LR-controlled verification.}
To rule out the LR confound (epoch-matched D\&R inherits the full-length schedule's LR trajectory), we retrain D\&R ($q{>}0.5$) with an independent linear schedule (2{,}533 steps, $\mathrm{LR} \to 0$).
The result ($17.651$) differs from the shared-schedule epoch-matched D\&R ($17.657 \pm 0.006$) by only $0.006$, confirming that LR schedule choice does not affect the epoch-confound finding.

